Subject: Compiled code calls the plain String.prototype methods without the native frame

What this does
  - `aot_lean_kind` also admits `at`, `charAt`, `charCodeAt`, `codePointAt`, `substring`,
    `substr`, `slice`, `indexOf`, `lastIndexOf`, `includes`, `startsWith`, `endsWith`, `trim`,
    `trimStart`, `trimEnd`, `toLowerCase` and `toUpperCase`. `qjs_aot_call_c` calls them
    directly when the receiver is a flat string and every argument is a number, a boolean,
    null, undefined or a flat string (no symbol, BigInt, object or rope: those can throw or run
    JS in ToString/ToInteger). A call with fewer arguments than the function declares gets the
    missing ones as undefined in a small local array, as the full call pads them.
  - `split`, `replace`, `replaceAll`, `match`, `search` and `localeCompare` are not admitted:
    they look up Symbol.split / Symbol.replace / ... on a string argument, which a script can
    define on String.prototype.

Why we need it
  The same frame setup and stack check as for the Map members (0357) on every string method
  call. string_indexof 944M -> 918M, string_upper 809M -> 774M, string_trim 762M -> 749M
  instructions compiled.

